{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound.wstd_ge_quarter_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound.wstd_ge_quarter_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WstdSuperExpBound.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**Algebraic transfer (B)+(D).** From the exact Plancherel identity\n`cube = 2·w_std + 2·e` (B, with `e = E_Planch[f^{λ/(3)}]`) together with `0 ≤ e` and the\ndominance `e ≤ w_std` (D), the tower weight carries at least a quarter of the cube moment:\n`cube ≤ 4·w_std`. Combined with a lower bound `L ≤ cube` (the pigeonhole `cube_sum_sq_ge`,\napplied with `L = √(k!)/p(k)^{3/2}`), this gives `L/4 ≤ w_std` — the super-exponential\nlower bound on `w_std`, modulo the (SYT-combinatorial) identity `cube = 2w+2e` and the\ninequality `e ≤ w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound.cube_sum_sq_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WstdSuperExpBound.cube_sum_sq_ge","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WstdSuperExpBound.lean#L29-L62","doc":"**Pigeonhole cube–square lower bound** (rpow-free form of `∑ aᵢ³ ≥ (S/N)^{3/2}`).\nFor a nonnegative real family `a : ι → ℝ` over a nonempty finite index type with `∑ aᵢ² = S`\nand `N = card ι`, the cube sum obeys `S³ ≤ N³·(∑ aᵢ³)²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}